 "note": "The 48 plain SRD 5.2.1 Beast stat blocks of CR 1/4 or lower (single creatures, type Beast), checked by Syndicate against the SRD 5.2.1 PDF on 2026-10-04 (tools-notes/pet-species-check-20261004.md). `state.py pet add` accepts these without a GM --override (rules/60 section 1, spec 9.2). Left out on purpose, so they need --override: swarms (Swarm of Bats/Rats/Ravens), Giant Fly and Giant Insect (item and spell stat blocks), and creatures that are not type Beast in 5.2.1 (Axe Beak, Flying Snake, Stirge, Giant Owl). Piranha and Seahorse cannot live out of water: legal, but the GM judges them. Old 5.1 names (Quipper, Sea Horse, Poisonous Snake, Giant Poisonous Snake) stay as aliases. GM-only; never shown to players, never read by /create. Aliases are reskins of the listed stat block (the GM may reskin a mastiff for a rottweiler).",
 "stat_fields": "Optional public SRD stat fields per species, shown on the owner's sheet card by tools/publisher.py when filled: ac (int), hp (int, average HP), attacks (list of {name, to_hit (int), damage (text)}; the card shows at most 2), traits (list of trait names; kept for the GM, not shown on the card). null / [] = not entered yet: the card then shows only the pet's name, kind and CR. Values must be checked against the SRD 5.2.1 PDF before they are entered. Entered so far (Syndicate, checked against SRD 5.2.1, 2026-10-06): cat, wolf.",
